# CMMC L1 / NIST 800-171 3.1.1 - Authorized principals at subscription scope
# Platform: Azure
# Check type: az_role_assignment_list across the subscription

META
    esp_id `cmmc-l1-3-1-1-az-rbac-principals-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `azure`
    criticality `high`

    category `asset_list`
    target_asset_type `Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions`

    title `CMMC L1 AC.L1-3.1.1: Authorized principals at Azure subscription scope`
    description `Validates that the Azure subscription has at least one role assignment recorded, demonstrating that access is gated by explicit RBAC grants rather than being implicit or unrestricted. Complements the M365::User + M365::RoleAssignment evidence already collected for this practice.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `azure,cmmc-l1,nist-800-171,3-1-1,ac,rbac,subscription-scope`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-171:3.1.1`
    control_objective `3.1.1`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `cloud-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Azure:subscription:rbac-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Verify the subscription has explicit RBAC role assignments at appropriate scopes. Every principal granted access must be a named User, ServicePrincipal, or Group. Investigate any assignment where principal_type is Unknown.`

    component_id `comp-azure-rbac`

    impl_3_1_1 `Access to Azure subscription resources is gated by role-based access control. Every principal granted access is explicitly assigned a defined role at a specific scope; principals without a role assignment cannot invoke management plane operations. Role assignments are inventoried as discrete Azure resources, allowing per-assignment audit. Together with the identity-tier controls in the directory service, this establishes the closed loop of authentication and authorization required for the practice.`

META_END

DEF
    # Replace the OBJECT below with one entry per Azure subscription you
    # want this policy to evaluate. The SET body is the part you customize;
    # everything else (STATE, CRI) stays as-is.
    SET subscriptions union
        OBJECT example_subscription
            name `ExampleSubscription`
            scope `subscription`
            subscription `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000`
        OBJECT_END
    SET_END

    STATE rbac_has_assignments
        found boolean = true
        role_count int >= 1
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN az_role_assignment_list
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF rbac_has_assignments
            SET_REF subscriptions
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
